Priya has judged skew from the widths of the two halves of the box ($5$ versus $10$), but skew is judged from the **whisker** lengths, not the box.
The left whisker runs from $5$ to $25$, a length of $20$. The right whisker runs from $40$ to $45$, a length of only $5$.
The left whisker is far longer, so the tail stretches to the left.
Negatively skewed — the opposite of Priya's claim.

